    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Madison comes for his preventive visit. He completed the health risk questionnaire beforehand. He started sertraline five weeks ago; he had mild nausea for the first week, which settled, and no other side effects, and he has missed no doses. He has finished seven of his twelve psychotherapy sessions and keeps his event diary: he has had two brief events in the five weeks since his last visit, both at the end of long study days, and he used his grounding steps to cut one short. He is sleeping about seven hours with a fixed bedtime. He has not driven since his first visit. He has had no thoughts of death or self-harm, and the rifle remains locked with the ammunition stored separately. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Preventive health visit, age 23</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Functional/dissociative seizures in psychotherapy; depression and anxiety on sertraline</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg each morning</td></tr><tr><td>Screening history</td><td>No HIV, hepatitis B, or hepatitis C test on record; childhood vaccines complete</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair, improving</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives alone on a rural property; close friends; studying for the law school admission test</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; one or two drinks a month (AUDIT-C 1); no drugs; walks daily; regular meals</td></tr><tr><td>Injury prevention</td><td>Seat belt always as a passenger; not driving at present; no swimming alone</td></tr><tr><td>Firearms</td><td>One rifle, locked, with ammunition stored separately</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Not sexually active in the past year; no known risk factors for sexually transmitted infection</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours with a fixed bedtime</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Dental</td><td>Dental check-up last year</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

